  "observation_id": "BIGFONT-KOREAN-001",
  "method": "Cell-to-syllable map derived from the marker build (BIGFONT-WORDS-002): each word's cell sequence was read straight off screen, so the mapping is solved as a constraint problem over shared cells rather than guessed.",
  "shared_cell_notes": [
    "02 (ー) appears in 5 of the 6 words, so it can only be blank -- every Korean reading drops the long-vowel mark.",
    "11 (ス) is the first syllable of スタート and the last of イエス; 스 satisfies both.",
    "01 (！) is shared by スタート！ and クリアー！.",
    "24 (ン) is left blank rather than reused for 티, because ン is the most common katakana and very likely appears in words not yet observed; a blank degrades gracefully, a reused syllable does not."
  ],
